\title{risikoR: Simulate, Analyse and Play the Board Game Risk}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

A toolkit for the board game Risk (German "Risiko"). Provides the dice-combat engine, single-battle and whole-conquest simulators, closed-form and Monte Carlo win probabilities, a full game state model with a world map and adjacency graph, scriptable artificial-intelligence agents, and a 'ggplot2' visualisation layer for maps, dice-duel outcomes and probability curves. An interactive 'shiny' application supports playing, simulating and analysing games. Combat resolution follows the standard rules in which the attacker rolls up to three dice and the defender up to two, comparing the highest dice pairwise with ties going to the defender.
}
